      "reasoning": "Nitpicks: Minor paraphrasing of doc text, and presenting the \u201cresult of the example\u201d as the inferred type shape (e.g., describing TodoPreview as having certain fields) would be fine if the agent clearly framed it as an inference from the code rather than claiming it was visibly displayed.\n\nCritical issues: (1) Exclude and Extract: screenshots show only TOC entries for Exclude/Extract, with no section body or example visible. Despite that, the agent reports their signatures/semantics and specific \u201cfirst displayed example and result\u201d for both. Given the task\u2019s hard constraint \u201cUse only visible TypeScript docs navigation and search\u201d and \u201caccording to the displayed examples,\u201d this is effectively unsupported/fabricated relative to what was actually visible in evidence. (2) Pick and Omit: while the Pick/Omit headings and example code blocks are visible, the screenshots do not show an expanded/evaluated type alias result like `type TodoPreview = { ... }`. The agent repeatedly claims the docs show an inline evaluated type result; evidence shows only `const todo: TodoPreview` as the visible hint/output line. That\u2019s a factual overclaim about what is displayed. (3) keyof page: action history indicates navigation to `/docs/handbook/2/keyof-types.html`, but no screenshot shows the keyof page or its examples; nonetheless the agent cites multiple specific displayed examples/results (Point/Arrayish/Mapish) as if seen. Under the task\u2019s \u201cdisplayed examples\u201d requirement, this is another unsupported claim.\n\nOutcome assessment: The agent did successfully reach the Utility Types page via TypeScript docs navigation (well-supported by screenshots). It also provides generally correct conceptual explanations of Pick vs Omit and their relationship to keyof. However, the task\u2019s primary deliverable is a comparison for all four utility types including the results of the first displayed example for each, plus an example-grounded explanation from the keyof page. Because Exclude/Extract example results (and even their section content) are not evidenced as viewed/visible, and the agent asserts displayed results that are not shown for Pick/Omit and not shown at all for keyof, the final delivered report does not meet the \u201conly visible docs / displayed examples\u201d constraint and misses/invalidates key required components. An average user relying on this output as \u201cwhat the docs showed\u201d would be misled, so the task is not successfully completed.",
